# Unauthorized Exit: "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. Surveil 1." It is an instant: on Bot2's turn 2 Bot1 returns its own Ornithopter (the
# opponent's is the other Exit scenario; a Mox Sapphire is nonland and is the same kind of target, a land is refused), then surveils 1 and keeps the Forest on top
# (CR 701.25a), so it is not in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Ornithopter
Unauthorized Exit
Island x3
Forest
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Unauthorized Exit.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Hand.Unauthorized Exit.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Forest)
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Island
? Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Island; Island; Island
? Bot1.Library.Top = Forest

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Unauthorized Exit
